#
# Stillwater, focus and do not disturb: quiet hours and focus modes over the
# notices zxvd keeps (notes.list, notes.mark_read), beside the app limits
# Shepherd sets (screen.status, screen.check). The anchor of layer 144: each
# entry is a general rule a later layer can repeat at its own scale.
#
#   quiet_now    a minute inside a daily window that may cross midnight:
#                from opens up to, not including, closes; opening after it
#                closes wraps past midnight (opens..1439 and 0..closes-1);
#                opening and closing at the same minute is the whole day.
#                The same rule zxvd keeps for an app's hours (zxv_screen.c,
#                from and to there), so one window means one thing.
#   let_through  let this notice through: a Watchfire emergency always; else
#                when not quiet, a sender on the allow list, or the same
#                caller twice within 3 minutes (gap 0..180 seconds; -1 none).
#   schedule_ok  what a schedule may hold: mode 0..2, days 0..127 (a mask,
#                bit 0 Monday), opens and closes 0..1439.
#   record_ok    a schedule makes a ^ZXQUIET record.
#
# The window's ends are named opens and closes, not from and to: TO is a
# COBOL reserved word, and one name serves every language.
#
# The task asked for the two rules in Eve and KRON. Eve only checks that a
# record's fields fit their declared ranges (zxapp_eve.c EV1-EV3); it cannot
# work out "in a quiet window now" or "let this notice through". So each rule
# is witnessed in Sutra and KRON instead (as Platen's copies_ok is), and Eve
# says what a schedule may hold. A row the two do not both answer the same
# way is held (BOTH). A Watchfire emergency is never held: the model lets it
# through before any other input is read (stillwater_model.c).
#
# Kept in C, since no runnable language owns it: matching a sender against
# the allow list (text), and which day's mask a window crossing midnight
# belongs to (the day it began). zxvd has no notice-filter method (the bus's
# do-not-disturb, zx_notify.h N6, is not reachable over RPC), so Stillwater
# decides what is held on its own side and changes nothing in zxvd but the
# read marks.
#
# Planned languages with no entry of their kind here: Racket (symbolic,
# parse), Mojo (numeric, ai), Perl (text, pattern); no pending line.
zxapp 1
id     stillwater
name   Stillwater
version 1.0.0
slot   144
layer  L1
icon   icons/l1/144-stillwater.svg
budget 233
needs  notify
needs  screen.time
model  apps/stillwater_model.c

provides quiet_now truth opens closes now
logic    sutra quiet_now apps/blocks/stillwater/quiet_now.sutra
logic    kron  quiet_now apps/blocks/stillwater/quiet_now.kron

provides let_through truth quiet allowed gap emergency
logic    sutra let_through apps/blocks/stillwater/let_through.sutra
logic    kron  let_through apps/blocks/stillwater/let_through.kron

provides schedule_ok truth mode days opens closes
logic    eve schedule_ok apps/blocks/stillwater/schedule.eve

provides record_ok truth schedule mode days opens closes allowed
logic    myra record_ok apps/blocks/stillwater/schedule.myra
